Agent: Yes — we decided on marigolds for your new plant.

Quick reminder and beginner care tips:
- Light: full sun (6+ hours/day) — they bloom best in bright light.  
- Soil: well-draining, average garden soil; marigolds aren’t picky about fertility.  
- Water: moderate — water at the base when top 1–2 inches dry; avoid constant soggy soil.  
- Planting: start seeds indoors 4–6 weeks before last frost or direct-sow after frost risk passes.  
- Spacing: 6–18 inches apart depending on variety (compact vs. tall).  
- Maintenance: deadhead spent blooms to encourage continuous flowering.  
- Pests/diseases: generally tough — watch for aphids or spider mites; good drainage prevents root rot.  
- Benefits: great companion plant in vegetable beds (deters some pests) and very beginner-friendly.

